//  PETPORTS -- LAMP MODULE EFFECT
//
//  MODELLED ON VANILLA'S lightaugment1, WITH ITS SCRIPT DELIBERATELY DROPPED.
//
//  That augment ships `lightaugment.lua`, whose entire body is
//
//      animator.setFlipped(mcontroller.facingDirection() == -1)
//
//  and it needs it because its light sits at [-1.0, 1.0] -- offset to one side
//  of the body, so an unflipped light would swap shoulders every time the
//  wearer turned around. Ours is centred on the body, where a mirror is the
//  identity, so the script would run three times a second to do nothing.
//
//  A CENTRED LIGHT IS ALSO THE RIGHT CHOICE FOR THIS FLEET, not just the cheap
//  one. Four chassis exist with more to come, their art is placeholder, and a
//  shoulder offset measured against the drone's current body would be wrong for
//  every one of them the first time a sprite changes size.
//
//  APPLIED PERSISTENTLY AND NEVER BY DURATION. The port calls
//  status.setPersistentEffects, which holds an effect for as long as it is in
//  the set and drops it the moment it leaves. `defaultDuration` is therefore
//  unread on the path we use -- it is stated anyway, at vanilla's value, so
//  that an effect applied some other way later behaves like the thing it was
//  copied from rather than expiring instantly.
//
//  THE COLOUR IS VANILLA'S, ON PURPOSE, FOR THIS FIRST TEST. [140,140,140] is
//  the value the reference augment ships. Tinting it to the chassis is an
//  obvious later polish, and doing it now would mean the first in-game check
//  could not distinguish "our effect works" from "our colour is wrong".

{
	"name" : "petports_module_light",

	"effectConfig" : {},

	"defaultDuration" : 5,

	"animationConfig" : "petports_module_light.animation"
}
